From: mayi <3363523343@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:22:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rtc): initialize power VBAT detect control to zero

[description ]:
- Initialize RTC_EN_PWR_VBAT_DET at 0x050260d0 with a full zero write
  in set_rtc_en_registers, matching the requested BF01 boot-time value.

[root   cause]:
- Clearing bit 2 preserves all other register bits and does not establish
  the requested zero value when those bits are set on entry.
- This records the initialization policy; it does not establish that
  this register caused any particular observed power-loss event.

[JIRA      ID]:N/A (BF01 integration)
[chip project]:181x
[side effects]:
- The change is in the common CV181X path, not a BF01-only conditional.
  All builds executing this initialization write the entire register.
- Other bits are deliberately not preserved. Other boards must review
  their RTC power design before reusing this policy.
- No ADC sampling threshold or Linux GPIO29 shutdown behavior changes.
- Rebuild FSBL and the corresponding FIP; replacing the application
  alone cannot update this boot-time register initialization.
- Patch replay is not an electrical or cold-boot power validation.

[Affected *.ko/*.so/*.a] :FSBL / FIP; no .ko/.so/.a
---
 plat/cv181x/platform.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plat/cv181x/platform.c b/plat/cv181x/platform.c
index 0073304..fdb10fd 100644
--- a/plat/cv181x/platform.c
+++ b/plat/cv181x/platform.c
@@ -639,7 +639,7 @@ void set_rtc_en_registers(void)
 	mmio_write_32(REG_RTC_CTRL_BASE + RTC_CTRL0, write_data);
 
 	// Avoid power up again after poweroff
-	mmio_clrbits_32(REG_RTC_BASE + RTC_EN_PWR_VBAT_DET, BIT(2));
+	mmio_write_32(REG_RTC_BASE + RTC_EN_PWR_VBAT_DET, 0x0);
 }
 
 void apply_analog_trimming_data(void)
